Job Description:
OVERVIEW OF JOB
Responsible for preparing and installing appliances, carrying out maintenance on all appliances, and employing electrical tools to carry out jobs within the company.
ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Installs, troubleshoots, repairs and overhauls household appliances;
Generates invoices for repairs of appliances;
Commissions new appliances at the customer’s location to ensure proper functioning;
Conducts functional test on appliances;
Coordinates with the main office and end users and provides product maintenance and support;
Works with company architect for kitchen layouts;
Works with site architect, plumbers and electricians in ensuring appliances are placed according to design plans;
Reviews all electrical circuit diagrams and test circuits to identify shortcircuits;
Ensures tidiness of work area;
Keeps records of all appliance checks and test results that are signed off with end users and properly filed;
Provides technical support and maintenance services;
Ensures all safety requirements are adhered to during installation or maintenance;
Ensures faults are reported promptly and repairs are carried out;
Repairs appliances properly and maintains minimum disbursal for parts;
Maintains the company vehicle properly and ensures proper records are kept;
Sends report on site observations and recommendations to technical supervisor;
Ensures accurate delivery records are kept;
Carry out electrical safety tests before and after every repair.
Key Requirements:
Qualification
BSc or HND in Electrical Electronics Engineering (compulsory)
Experience in electrical analysis and electronics
Experience in troubleshooting
Experience in reading electrical circuit
Knowledgeable in theoretical and practical electrical engineering Work Experience
1–3 years extensive hands-on work experience as a technician (in electrical/electronics)
